parameters.text:
=Analyze the supplied search results and identify the three most relevant direct competitors for the product.

PROJECT CONTEXT

Project ID:
{{ $json.project_id }}

Project name:
{{ $json.project_name }}

Research goal:
{{ $json.research_goal }}

Product description:
{{ $json.product_description }}

SEARCH RESULTS

{{ JSON.stringify($json.search_results) }}

TASK

1. Read all supplied search results.
2. Extract real companies or products mentioned in the evidence.
3. Ignore article titles, publications, reports, lists, agencies, directories, case studies and generic categories.
4. Select exactly three competitors when sufficient evidence is available.
5. Prioritize competitors that:
   - offer the same or a highly similar core product;
   - solve a similar user problem;
   - target comparable users;
   - operate in the same or a relevant geographic market;
   - provide a comparable digital product experience.
6. For digital banking products, prioritize digital banks and neobanks over products focused mainly on cryptocurrency, budgeting, transfers or payment processing.
7. For each selected competitor:
   - provide its exact company or product name;
   - explain why it is relevant;
   - identify the source title and source URL supporting the selection;
   - provide a confidence score between 0 and 1.
8. Do not invent an official company URL. Use the URL of the supplied search result as source_url.
9. Do not make claims that are not supported by the supplied search results.
10. If fewer than three strong direct competitors are supported, select the best available candidates and lower their confidence scores.
11. Return only the required structured output.

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "project_id": "bank-onboarding-2026",
  "competitors": [
    {
      "competitor_name": "N26",
      "selection_rationale": "N26 offers mobile-first bank account opening and digital account management for customers in Germany.",
      "source_title": "German challenger banks: who's who",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/source",
      "confidence": 0.91
    },
    {
      "competitor_name": "Revolut",
      "selection_rationale": "Revolut provides digital financial accounts and mobile onboarding for a comparable European user group.",
      "source_title": "European digital banking companies",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/source",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "competitor_name": "bunq",
      "selection_rationale": "bunq is a European mobile bank with fully digital account creation and account management.",
      "source_title": "European challenger banks overview",
      "source_url": "https://example.com/source",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "selection_summary": "The selected competitors provide comparable mobile-first banking services and digital account onboarding for European users.",
  "overall_confidence": 0.85
}

